1
00:05:50,526 --> 00:05:56,526
Hedda Gabler is a drama film directed by Matthew John.

2
00:11:41,052 --> 00:11:47,052
Hedda, beautiful daughter of the late General Gabler, returns from her honeymoon with
scholar husband Jorgen to confront the boredom and banality of married life.

3
00:17:31,578 --> 00:17:37,578
Although she has little more than amused contempt for her husband, she is pregnant by him and is revolted by
the thought of carrying his child and the changes that motherhood will impose upon her future.

4
00:23:22,105 --> 00:23:28,105
When the re-appearance of an old flame of hers threatens both Jorgen's career prospects and her own amour propre,
Hedda contrives to bring about Lovborg's destruction but, in the process, also brings about her own.

5
00:29:12,631 --> 00:29:18,631
Hedda Gabler, played by Rita Ramnani.

6
00:35:03,157 --> 00:35:09,157
Ejlert Løvborg, played by Francisco Ortiz.

7
00:40:53,684 --> 00:40:59,684
Hedda Gabler is a film based on the 1891 Victorian period play Hedda
Gabler, written by Norwegian playwright Henrik Ibsen.

8
00:46:44,210 --> 00:46:50,210
One of many adaptations of this play, the film Hedda Gabler was
produced, adapted, and directed by Matthew John.

9
00:52:34,736 --> 00:52:40,736
Hedda Gabler is an example of realism in nineteenth-century playwriting, and
is one of the world's best known and most performed dramas.

10
00:58:25,263 --> 00:58:31,263
The film was shot at Maunsel House.

11
01:04:15,789 --> 01:04:21,789
The movie premiered at the Vika Cinema, Oslo on 8 September
2016 to open the Ibsen International Festivalen.

12
01:10:06,315 --> 01:10:12,315
A press launch at the Henrik Ibsen Museum on 9 September 2016.

13
01:15:56,842 --> 01:16:02,842
the event was sponsored by H+M and Radisson Blu.

14
01:21:47,368 --> 01:21:53,368
Matthew John attended the red carpet with Swedish
supermodel Marcus Schenkenberg.

15
01:27:37,894 --> 01:27:43,894
The title role is played by Rita Ramnani.

16
01:33:28,421 --> 01:33:34,421
The film is also part of the Worcester University PR and Journalism programme.

17
